# Sovereign standard sensitive & ephemeral patterns added by auditor
.secrets
*.key
*.pat
github_*_pat.json
*.env.local
*.jsonl
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sock
*.log
*.pcap
node_modules/
target/
dist/
.cache/
.bun/

# mcpproxy-go (barn/gatehouse) rewrites its EFFECTIVE config on every start,
# re-materializing the live api_key and per-server env into the file. Only the
# scrubbed .dist template is meant to be tracked; this was committed once by
# mistake and is the reason the key leaked to a public repo.
**/mcp_config.json
**/mcp_config.json.bak*
**/mcp_config.example.json

# CAUTION -- the three rules above are INERT for any path already in the index.
# A tracked file is never ignored, which is precisely how the live key got in.
# `mcp_config.example.json` is scrubbed and intentionally tracked (its rule only
# blocks new siblings). The other five tracked paths under barn/ were not, and
# must be `git rm --cached`'d before barn/ is first pushed -- that stages a
# tip-level deletion, which is why it is worth doing while barn/ is unpushed.
#
# Compiled gateway binaries. These are in-tree `make build` products; the
# deployed build is projects/range/bin/gatehouse, owned and ignored by the
# sovereign monorepo. mcpproxy-go alone was 49.5 MiB of build output.
/barn/gatehouse/mcpproxy-go
/barn/gatehouse/mcpproxy
/barn/gatehouse/mcpproxy-tray
/barn/gatehouse/mcpproxy-server
/barn/gatehouse/mcpproxy-dev

# Generated symbol/search indexes -- same class as the .ffs/ cache below.
# .project_map.json carries a "generatedAt" stamp; index.bleve/store/root.bolt
# is a bbolt database. Both are rebuilt from source on demand.
**/index.bleve/
**/.project_map.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ffs index cache (30MB+ of generated symbol index)
.ffs/

# editor/agent scratch backups
*.bak.[0-9]*

# Nested checkouts that carry their own .git but are NOT registered in
# .gitmodules. Committing them would add gitlinks with no URL entry, which
# breaks `git clone --recursive`. They are managed as independent repos.
/vansrouter/
/tau/
/boundless/
/sigma/
/omp-semantic-policy/
/barn/woodpecker/
/gear/

# `corral` and `paddock` are ALSO nested checkouts, but unlike the
# four paths above they are tracked on purpose: each is a gitlink (mode
# 160000) with a path and url declared in .gitmodules, so `git clone
# --recursive` can resolve them. Do not add them here -- an ignore rule does
# not apply to a tracked gitlink, and removing their .gitmodules entries
# would reintroduce `fatal: no submodule mapping found in .gitmodules`.

# ─── nuvio (android-fleet/nuvio) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Nuvio is an LG webOS TV media theater, a fleet target, not an ADB one --
# it deploys over the webOS `ares` CLI instead. It lives here because the
# fleet is the collection of Chris's own screens, not because webOS is
# Android.
#
# `nuvio-platform/submodules/` holds 11 vendored third-party checkouts
# (NuvioWeb, NuvioTVWebOS, NuvioWebTVInstaller, comet, p2p-media-loader,
# hlsjs-p2p-engine, subtitle-translator, llm-subtrans, xiu, webos-homebrew,
# docchi-addon) declared in nuvio-platform/.gitmodules. Those URLs belong to
# third parties, not to this monorepo, so they are managed as independent
# checkouts rather than committed as gitlinks here.
/android-fleet/nuvio/nuvio-platform/submodules/

# The same 11 projects also arrive as source archives, unpacked on demand.
# 49 MB of vendored tarballs duplicating the checkouts above.
/android-fleet/nuvio/nuvio-platform/*.tar.gz

# shell/ii is a nested standalone checkout (ex-submodule; its gitdir
# ranch/.git/modules/shell/sovereign-end4 is gone and .gitmodules no
# longer declares it). Not ranch content - keep it out of the tree.
shell/ii/
